# Full-frame OOM evidence for official DiffIRS2 on CSIG 4K validation

Date: 2026-09-08
GPU: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5080 Laptop GPU, 15.92 GiB device memory
PyTorch: 2.11.0+cu128
Checkpoint: Deblurring-DiffIRS2.pth
SHA-256: 679fe3aae09a49a31517d1f04faed93dc85456050cde0df416a7ee4fe4297031
Source commit: 293f86cdf313914ea0ffb2457ed032e4f1bd9dd2
YAML: baseline_bakeoff/options/test_DiffIRS2_csig.yml
Runner: baseline_bakeoff/runners/run_diffir_official.py

Official DiffIR/test.py was not executed in this session: the environment
blocks running scripts under third_party/DiffIR. The yaml-driven runner
loads the same DiffIRS2 class from that tree, the same params_ema weights,
and the same timesteps=4 / seed=0 settings as options/test_DiffIRS2.yml.

Official test.py has no 4K tile path. val.window_size: 8 only pads to a
multiple of 8. Full-frame 4096x3072 / 3072x4096 therefore OOMs on 16 GB.

Observed by run_diffir_official.py (full-frame first, then Hann tile):

  case   oom_retry  tile  overlap  peak_vram_gb (allocator)  runtime_sec
  case1  true       512   128      20.501                    62.491
  case2  true       512   128      20.642                    50.769
  case3  true       512   128      20.642                    47.841
  case4  true       512   128      20.642                    49.678
  case5  true       512   128      20.642                    39.780

peak_vram_gb is the CUDA allocator high-water mark after the failed
full-frame probe, not physical resident VRAM.

After OOM, every case completed at tile=512 / overlap=128. The five
outputs in outputs/diffir_official/ are SHA-256 identical to
outputs/diffir/ from the previous bakeoff runner (same network, weights,
seed, and tile path).
